{
  "_comment": [
    "The answers the catalog seed cannot give, maintained by hand.",
    "",
    "worker/scripts/ knows what an ingredient is, how it is stored, what",
    "opening does to it and who delivers it. It does not know any of the",
    "following, and nothing in the repository does:",
    "",
    "allergens      Generated by import_allergens.py from the kitchen's own",
    "               Allergen Matrix in the forms repository. Do not edit by",
    "               hand: re-run the importer. An allergen line is a",
    "               compliance statement, so it comes from the document that",
    "               is maintained as one and from nowhere else. Items the",
    "               matrix does not cover are absent here and print 'Not",
    "               recorded' rather than a guess.",
    "",
    "may_contain    Also generated. Where the matrix names a cross-contact",
    "               allergen the label names it, and still ends 'and other",
    "               allergens'.",
    "",
    "products       Per finished product: whether it carries the oval health mark,",
    "               the customer SKU and the pack quantity for the packet and the",
    "               case, and a label_name where the label does not simply use the",
    "               catalog name. The 'M&R' prefix the earlier artwork carried was",
    "               dropped (Dean, 2026-09-01), which is why most products need no",
    "               label_name at all.",
    "",
    "health_mark is stated for every product, true or false, and never left",
    "unset. The catalog holds null for all of them, which means nobody had",
    "determined it; Dean determined it on 2026-09-01 -- the two broths and the",
    "four frozen ramen carry the oval, and nothing else does. A wrongly-absent",
    "mark and a considered absence have to stay distinguishable when an auditor",
    "asks, which is why false is written out rather than assumed."
  ],
